1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,910
You can lose money,

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:05,430
change jobs, start over from scratch…

3
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:07,880
but there's one thing no one

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:11,260
can take from you: the person you've become.

5
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,480
Hello, my friend.

6
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:15,750
Welcome to Cozy French Radio.

7
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,700
It's Lia, and I'm really happy to spend

8
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,320
this little moment with you.

9
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,750
Tell me, how are you feeling today?

10
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:26,150
Did you have a nice day?

11
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,240
Or did you spend a lot of time

12
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,530
taking care of others,

13
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:31,950
your work, your responsibilities…

14
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,640
without really thinking about yourself?

15
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:37,800
Maybe you're listening to this on your way home.

16
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,420
Maybe you're making dinner.

17
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:42,610
Or maybe you're just sitting somewhere,

18
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:45,720
with a few quiet minutes ahead of you.

19
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,560
This morning, I found an old notebook in a drawer.

20
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,990
Inside, there were a few ideas I had

21
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:54,990
written down a long time ago.

22
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,570
Some had come true.

23
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:59,120
Others had stayed simple plans.

24
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,650
And looking at those pages,

25
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:03,860
I thought of something.

26
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,590
We spend a lot of time building our life.

27
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:10,360
But how much time do we spend building ourselves?

28
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:14,810
That's a question I'd like to explore with you today.

29
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:17,760
We're going to talk about a very simple idea:

30
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,400
investing in yourself.

31
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,190
And while you listen to me,

32
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:24,330
you can also practise your French calmly.

33
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:26,500
You'll hear everyday words,

34
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,300
useful expressions and questions you can

35
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,320
ask yourself in your own life.

36
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:34,350
You don't need to understand everything perfectly.

37
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:38,320
Just listen, like a conversation between two friends.

38
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:42,670
Now, imagine someone who works a lot.

39
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:45,240
Every morning, she wakes up early.

40
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,550
She makes her coffee,

41
00:01:46,550 --> 00:01:49,460
takes public transport and spends the day at the office.

42
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,990
She's careful with her spending.

43
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:54,820
She saves up to buy a new car,

44
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:58,880
a flat, or just to feel a bit more secure.

45
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,800
And that's a good thing.

46
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:04,520
But one evening, she comes home, tired.

47
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:08,050
She sees a book she bought several months earlier.

48
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:10,750
She wanted to learn something new.

49
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,550
Maybe a foreign language.

50
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:15,200
Maybe a skill for her job.

51
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,900
But every time she looks at that book,

52
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:20,510
she tells herself: "I don't have time."

53
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:22,740
So she picks up her phone.

54
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:24,910
She watches a few videos.

55
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:26,250
An hour goes by.

56
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:26,850
Then two.

57
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:28,400
And the book stays closed.

58
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,000
Maybe you know this situation.

59
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,080
We find time for lots of things,

60
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:37,000
but we sometimes struggle to find any for ourselves.

61
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,430
And here's what's interesting.

62
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:44,050
We often think investing means spending money to

63
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:45,800
earn more later.

64
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,180
But investing in yourself

65
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:50,090
isn't only about money.

66
00:02:50,090 --> 00:02:53,870
It's also choosing what can help us grow.

67
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,660
Learning something.

68
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,840
Taking care of our health.

69
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,750
Building our confidence.

70
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:04,320
Or simply understanding better what matters to us.

71
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,360
Because in the end,

72
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:08,410
the things we buy can get old.

73
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:10,320
Our situation can change.

74
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:12,500
But the things we learn,

75
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,690
the experiences we live and the qualities

76
00:03:15,690 --> 00:03:19,200
we develop can stay with us.

77
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:22,590
You don't need to be rich to invest in yourself.

78
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:25,230
You don't need a perfect life.

79
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:27,810
You can start with ten minutes,

80
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,560
a small effort or a simple decision.

81
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:33,990
And maybe the best investment isn't the one

82
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:36,680
that instantly changes what you own.

83
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:40,180
It's the one that gently changes who you become.

84
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,140
Imagine that every morning,

85
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:45,000
someone gives you a little box.

86
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,760
In this box, there are twenty-four coins.

87
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:54,440
Each coin stands for one hour of your day.

88
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:57,320
You can use these coins however you like.

89
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,600
To work.

90
00:03:58,600 --> 00:03:59,870
To sleep.

91
00:03:59,870 --> 00:04:00,670
To eat.

92
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,990
To talk with someone you love.

93
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:03,920
To learn.

94
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,400
Or simply to do nothing.

95
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,600
But there's one rule.

96
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,500
At the end of the day,

97
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:14,120
all the coins disappear.

98
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,360
You can't keep them for tomorrow.

99
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,210
You can't get them back.

100
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:19,400
And the next morning,

101
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,760
you get a new box.

102
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,800
It's a bit like our time,

103
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,190
don't you think?

104
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:29,820
We all get twenty-four hours a day.

105
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:32,840
Of course, we don't all have the same responsibilities

106
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,900
or the same freedom to use them.

107
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:37,780
Some people have to work very long hours.

108
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,180
Others take care of their children,

109
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:43,480
their parents or someone who needs help.

110
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:46,350
And sometimes, after all those obligations,

111
00:04:46,350 --> 00:04:48,280
there's very little time left for yourself.

112
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,880
So I won't tell you that all you need

113
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:55,050
is to organise your day better to solve all your problems.

114
00:04:55,050 --> 00:04:57,320
Life is more complicated than that.

115
00:04:57,370 --> 00:05:00,190
But there's an interesting question.

116
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:05,280
What do we do with the time we can truly choose?

117
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:09,870
Imagine someone coming home after work.

118
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:11,400
She's tired.

119
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:15,230
She sits down on her sofa and opens her phone.

120
00:05:15,230 --> 00:05:18,360
She just wants to relax for five minutes.

121
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:21,000
But one video becomes ten videos.

122
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,720
Ten videos become an hour.

123
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:26,420
And when she looks at the clock,

124
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:27,550
she feels frustrated.

125
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:28,590
She wanted to read.

126
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:30,100
She wanted to call a friend.

127
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:32,300
She wanted to practise her French.

128
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,800
But now, she's too tired.

129
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,310
The problem isn't having watched videos.

130
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:41,230
We all need some entertainment.

131
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:44,930
The problem is when a habit takes our time

132
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:47,440
without us really choosing it.

133
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,880
Do you see the difference?

134
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:52,040
Resting for an hour because you

135
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:54,180
need it is a decision.

136
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,750
Spending an hour doing something that

137
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:57,610
you don't even enjoy anymore,

138
00:05:57,610 --> 00:06:00,630
just out of habit, is something else.

139
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:03,240
And that difference matters.

140
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:06,140
We often pay attention to our money.

141
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,750
Before buying something,

142
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:10,600
we ask ourselves: "Do I really need it?"

143
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,970
But we don't always ask that question

144
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:15,600
about our time.

145
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,480
"Does this activity give me anything?"

146
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,510
"Did I choose it?"

147
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:23,510
"Do I want to keep going?"

148
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:26,440
These questions aren't here to make you feel guilty.

149
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,260
Quite the opposite.

150
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,240
They can help you get back a bit of freedom.

151
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:33,880
And here's a paradox I'd like to share with you.

152
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:36,320
To use your time better,

153
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:39,750
you don't always need to do more.

154
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:42,440
Sometimes, you need to do less,

155
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,440
but choose more.

156
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:47,890
You can decide to spend fifteen minutes on

157
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,870
something that matters to you.

158
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:51,160
Reading a few pages.

159
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,610
Writing in a notebook.

160
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:53,930
Going for a walk.

161
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:55,510
Or listening to French,

162
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:56,560
like you're doing now.

163
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:59,360
Fifteen minutes doesn't seem like much.

164
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:03,560
But it's fifteen minutes you chose for yourself.

165
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:07,200
And it can change the way you see your day.

166
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,630
Because your time isn't just something

167
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:11,690
that you spend.

168
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:14,960
It's also a part of your life that you build.

169
00:07:15,010 --> 00:07:18,270
So, tonight, maybe you can ask yourself

170
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:20,040
a little question.

171
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:24,600
"Today, what truly deserved my time?"

172
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:28,690
There's no right or wrong answer.

173
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:32,400
Just a chance to better understand what matters to you.

174
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:36,210
There are doors we can't see…

175
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:40,190
until we've learned something new.

176
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:43,110
It's an idea I find fascinating.

177
00:07:43,110 --> 00:07:45,650
Because when we learn,

178
00:07:45,650 --> 00:07:49,600
we don't always know where that learning will lead us.

179
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:54,720
Imagine a young woman who works at a small company.

180
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,870
She does her job seriously.

181
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:59,080
She's kind to her colleagues.

182
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,120
But she'd like to discover other possibilities.

183
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:06,140
One day, she decides to learn French.

184
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:08,610
Not to get a new job right away.

185
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:11,190
Not because someone asks her to.

186
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:14,000
Simply because she loves the language.

187
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,760
At first, it's hard.

188
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,090
She forgets words.

189
00:08:18,090 --> 00:08:19,630
She mixes up verbs.

190
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:23,480
She listens to a conversation and understands almost nothing.

191
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:28,160
Sometimes she thinks: "I'm too old to learn."

192
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,800
Other times: "I'm not talented enough."

193
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,740
But she keeps going.

194
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:34,640
Ten minutes on some days.

195
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:37,330
Twenty minutes when she has more time.

196
00:08:37,330 --> 00:08:39,020
She listens to podcasts,

197
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:43,000
repeats sentences and writes a few expressions in a notebook.

198
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:47,680
After several months, she starts to understand more.

199
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,990
One day, at work,

200
00:08:48,990 --> 00:08:50,610
a colleague asks her:

201
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:52,420
"Do you speak French?"

202
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:55,680
She answers shyly: "A little bit."

203
00:08:55,680 --> 00:09:00,240
Her colleague explains that a French-speaking client is looking for someone

204
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:03,000
to help them communicate.

205
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:03,850
She hesitates.

206
00:09:03,850 --> 00:09:05,960
She isn't perfectly bilingual.

207
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,080
But she agrees to try, with her team's help.

208
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:13,760
And this small experience makes her want to keep learning.

209
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:19,040
Maybe later she'll discover new career opportunities.

210
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,960
Maybe not.

211
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:23,400
But something has already changed.

212
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:27,950
She has discovered an ability she didn't know she had.

213
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:30,600
And that discovery gives her confidence.

214
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:34,200
That's what I call an invisible door.

215
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:39,220
Before learning, she didn't even know this possibility existed.

216
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:43,480
And you know, this doesn't only happen with foreign languages.

217
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:47,910
Learning to cook can change your relationship with food.

218
00:09:47,910 --> 00:09:52,410
Learning to communicate better can transform a relationship.

219
00:09:52,410 --> 00:09:56,840
Learning to manage a budget can bring you more peace of mind.

220
00:09:56,840 --> 00:10:00,820
And learning to understand your emotions can change the

221
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,760
way you react in difficult moments.

222
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:08,320
Every new skill can make your world a little bigger.

223
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:11,640
But there's something I'd like to point out.

224
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:17,480
You don't have to turn every bit of learning into career success.

225
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:21,400
You also have the right to learn just for fun.

226
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:25,550
You can learn to draw because it relaxes you.

227
00:10:25,550 --> 00:10:29,360
You can discover music because it makes you happy.

228
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:32,240
You can study a language because you love

229
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,280
hearing its sounds.

230
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:37,440
Not everything has to become a way to make money.

231
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:41,440
Sometimes, learning is already a lovely reward.

232
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,140
And there's another important truth.

233
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:46,280
When we're beginners,

234
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:49,360
we have to accept not knowing everything.

235
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,600
It's sometimes uncomfortable.

236
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:54,240
We'd like to speak perfectly.

237
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,330
Understand right away.

238
00:10:56,330 --> 00:10:58,640
Succeed on the very first try.

239
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:02,280
But learning also means making mistakes.

240
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:05,300
And mistakes aren't necessarily proof

241
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,920
that we're bad at it.

242
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:10,840
They often show that we're trying something new.

243
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,400
Think about your French.

244
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,860
Maybe a few months ago,

245
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,800
some sentences seemed impossible to you.

246
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:21,600
Today, you understand them more easily.

247
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,310
This progress may be quiet.

248
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:25,920
But it's real.

249
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,880
So don't only measure what you

250
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,050
don't know yet.

251
00:11:30,050 --> 00:11:33,640
Look also at what you're able to do now.

252
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:37,570
Because sometimes we move forward so slowly that we

253
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:40,740
forget to notice how far we've already come.

254
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:44,600
And a skill you develop today can become,

255
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:48,030
tomorrow, a possibility you never imagined.

256
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:51,870
We sometimes have a strange idea of success.

257
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:54,100
We think that to move forward,

258
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,150
we always have to be busy.

259
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:57,720
Working more.

260
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,800
Sleeping less.

261
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,310
Making more effort.

262
00:12:00,310 --> 00:12:02,310
Filling every minute.

263
00:12:02,310 --> 00:12:05,920
But if you keep going without ever

264
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:08,340
resting, what happens?

265
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:11,880
At some point, your body and your mind start

266
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:13,400
asking for a break.

267
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:17,760
Imagine someone with a lot of responsibilities.

268
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:18,830
She gets up early,

269
00:12:18,830 --> 00:12:23,190
works all day and looks after her family in the evening.

270
00:12:23,190 --> 00:12:25,730
When someone asks how she's doing,

271
00:12:25,730 --> 00:12:26,870
she answers: "I'm fine,

272
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:28,760
just a little tired."

273
00:12:28,810 --> 00:12:32,930
But this tiredness has lasted for several weeks.

274
00:12:32,930 --> 00:12:34,130
She sleeps badly.

275
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:36,160
She eats quickly.

276
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:39,110
She almost never has a quiet moment.

277
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:41,340
And yet, she keeps telling herself:

278
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:43,920
"I'll rest when I've finished everything

279
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:44,680
I have to do."

280
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:49,600
The problem is, her list never ends.

281
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:52,160
There's always something to do.

282
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,680
A message to send.

283
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,000
A task to finish.

284
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,770
A problem to solve.

285
00:12:56,770 --> 00:13:01,960
So rest becomes a reward she never manages to get.

286
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:05,470
Maybe you know this feeling.

287
00:13:05,470 --> 00:13:08,870
Sometimes we act as if taking care of

288
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,800
ourselves were a waste of time.

289
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:15,420
As if sleeping enough mattered less than working.

290
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:19,810
As if a walk were useless because it produces nothing.

291
00:13:19,810 --> 00:13:24,140
As if saying no to a request were proof of selfishness.

292
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,840
But let's think for a moment.

293
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:30,600
If your phone is almost out of battery, what do you do?

294
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,820
You plug it in.

295
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:35,620
You don't ask it to work even faster.

296
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:38,160
You understand that it needs energy.

297
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:41,230
So why do we sometimes struggle to accept the

298
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:43,200
same thing for ourselves?

299
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:45,780
Of course, we're not machines.

300
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:48,960
And our needs are much more complex.

301
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:52,390
But this comparison reminds us of something simple.

302
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:55,560
We can't keep giving our energy

303
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:58,610
without also taking time to get it back.

304
00:13:58,610 --> 00:14:03,140
Taking care of yourself isn't a pause in your life.

305
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,080
It's a part of your life.

306
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,480
You don't need to earn rest by

307
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,690
becoming completely exhausted.

308
00:14:09,690 --> 00:14:13,440
You can rest simply because you're human.

309
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:16,790
And investing in yourself doesn't only mean developing

310
00:14:16,790 --> 00:14:18,800
new skills.

311
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,330
It also means protecting your health,

312
00:14:21,330 --> 00:14:23,360
your sleep and your balance.

313
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:27,550
Sometimes, the best choice for your future is to go

314
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:29,110
to bed a little earlier.

315
00:14:29,110 --> 00:14:32,920
Sometimes, it's making a simple, pleasant meal.

316
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:36,430
Sometimes, it's walking outside for a few minutes.

317
00:14:36,430 --> 00:14:38,630
And sometimes, it's saying:

318
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:41,940
"Today, I can't do any more."

319
00:14:41,940 --> 00:14:44,760
That sentence can be hard to say.

320
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,090
Especially if you're used to saying yes to

321
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:48,130
everyone.

322
00:14:48,130 --> 00:14:50,550
But having limits doesn't mean that you're

323
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,110
a bad person.

324
00:14:52,110 --> 00:14:55,520
You can love others and take care of yourself.

325
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:58,520
You can be generous and admit that you

326
00:14:58,520 --> 00:14:59,560
need rest.

327
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:03,260
You can have big ambitions without sacrificing every

328
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:04,490
quiet moment.

329
00:15:04,490 --> 00:15:09,810
And maybe that's one of the most important investments.

330
00:15:09,810 --> 00:15:13,460
Learning to build a life where you can move forward…

331
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,240
without losing yourself along the way.

332
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:18,680
I'd like you to ask yourself a question.

333
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:22,440
"If I treated my body and my mind like

334
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,770
something precious,

335
00:15:23,770 --> 00:15:26,400
what would I do differently today?"

336
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:30,760
Maybe the answer will be simple.

337
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,270
Drinking a glass of water.

338
00:15:32,270 --> 00:15:34,120
Closing your computer.

339
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,440
Going out for some fresh air.

340
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:38,200
Or accepting that, for today,

341
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,230
you've already done enough.

342
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:44,000
Imagine you could meet the person you'll

343
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,560
be in five years.

344
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:49,600
Not in some extraordinary dream.

345
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:52,130
Just in a quiet little café.

346
00:15:52,130 --> 00:15:56,160
You arrive, open the door and see

347
00:15:56,160 --> 00:16:00,030
that person sitting by the window.

348
00:16:00,030 --> 00:16:01,030
It's you.

349
00:16:01,030 --> 00:16:02,810
A little older.

350
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:06,050
With a few more experiences.

351
00:16:06,050 --> 00:16:08,750
Maybe a few new habits.

352
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:12,520
Maybe a different way of looking at life.

353
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:15,520
You sit down across from that person.

354
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,320
And you ask them a question.

355
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:21,120
"Are you happy with what we've built?"

356
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:25,360
Now imagine they answer: "Yes.

357
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,710
Not because everything is perfect.

358
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:31,010
But because we've learned to take better

359
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:32,280
care of ourselves."

360
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,820
I find that image interesting.

361
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,300
Because when we talk about investing in ourselves,

362
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:41,230
we often think about becoming someone extraordinary.

363
00:16:41,230 --> 00:16:41,820
Richer.

364
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:43,150
Smarter.

365
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:44,360
More impressive.

366
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,360
More admired.

367
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:48,220
But is that really the goal?

368
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:53,450
Do we just want to look impressive to other people?

369
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:57,430
Or do we want to build a life where we feel good?

370
00:16:57,430 --> 00:16:59,960
It's not always the same thing.

371
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,720
Imagine two people.

372
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:04,220
The first one works non-stop.

373
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:06,520
She wants to succeed quickly.

374
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,610
She constantly compares her progress with other people's.

375
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:12,280
Every time she reaches a goal,

376
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,580
she immediately picks a new one.

377
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:17,410
She almost never takes the time to appreciate what

378
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:19,100
she has achieved.

379
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,880
The second person has dreams too.

380
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:26,310
She works, she learns and she makes an effort.

381
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:29,830
But she also takes the time to see her progress.

382
00:17:29,830 --> 00:17:33,680
She accepts that some days are less productive.

383
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:36,600
She tries to build sincere relationships.

384
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,770
And she understands that her worth doesn't depend

385
00:17:38,770 --> 00:17:40,480
only on her results.

386
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,800
Which of these two people has truly invested in herself?

387
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:48,260
Maybe both, in a way.

388
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:52,150
But the second one understood something essential.

389
00:17:52,150 --> 00:17:55,560
The person we become is just as important as

390
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,360
the things we get.

391
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:01,000
Because you can reach a big goal and

392
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,740
still feel empty.

393
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:07,560
You can earn more money and still lack peace of mind.

394
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:11,190
You can get lots of compliments and keep

395
00:18:11,190 --> 00:18:12,400
doubting yourself.

396
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:16,510
Outward success can be important.

397
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:18,860
But it doesn't replace the relationship you

398
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:20,160
build with yourself.

399
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,460
So, when you think about your future,

400
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:26,680
try not to look only at what you want to own.

401
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:30,710
Also ask yourself: "How do I want to feel?"

402
00:18:30,710 --> 00:18:34,210
"What qualities do I want to develop?"

403
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:37,060
"What kind of person do I want to be

404
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:38,510
with the people I love?"

405
00:18:38,510 --> 00:18:41,520
Maybe you want to become more patient.

406
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,590
More curious.

407
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:44,840
Calmer when things get hard.

408
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:48,850
Or simply learn to trust yourself more.

409
00:18:48,850 --> 00:18:50,290
And you know what?

410
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:53,400
You don't need to wait five years to start.

411
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:56,680
You can make a small choice today.

412
00:18:56,680 --> 00:19:00,750
A choice that looks like the person you'd like to become.

413
00:19:00,750 --> 00:19:03,670
If you want to be more curious,

414
00:19:03,670 --> 00:19:05,300
learn something.

415
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,220
If you want to be more present,

416
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,260
really listen to someone.

417
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,910
If you want to be calmer,

418
00:19:10,910 --> 00:19:13,720
take a moment before reacting.

419
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:15,950
And if you want to be braver,

420
00:19:15,950 --> 00:19:19,400
try something you've been putting off for a long time,

421
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:22,830
at your own pace and without taking needless risks.

422
00:19:22,830 --> 00:19:25,140
These are small gestures.

423
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:29,000
But they say something about the direction you're choosing.

424
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,560
And here's a thought I'd like you to keep.

425
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:36,060
You don't need to become perfect to be

426
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:37,320
proud of yourself.

427
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:39,620
You can be proud of the way you

428
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:41,030
keep on learning.

429
00:19:41,030 --> 00:19:46,430
You can be proud of starting again after a hard time.

430
00:19:46,430 --> 00:19:48,530
Proud of having asked for help.

431
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:51,820
Proud of having tried something new.

432
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:55,880
Proud of realising that an old habit wasn't doing

433
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,620
you any good anymore.

434
00:19:56,620 --> 00:20:01,490
Your future isn't built only on big decisions.

435
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:04,510
It's also built in those ordinary moments when

436
00:20:04,510 --> 00:20:07,710
you choose to respect yourself a little more.

437
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:09,970
And one day, maybe,

438
00:20:09,970 --> 00:20:12,630
you'll look back with tenderness.

439
00:20:12,630 --> 00:20:15,760
You won't see someone who succeeded at everything.

440
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:19,910
You'll see someone who kept on growing.

441
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:23,420
And that already deserves a lot of respect.

442
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:24,930
Before we say goodbye,

443
00:20:24,930 --> 00:20:28,300
I'd like to come back to a very simple idea.

444
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:31,810
Investing in yourself doesn't mean you have to

445
00:20:31,810 --> 00:20:33,670
become someone else.

446
00:20:33,670 --> 00:20:36,380
You're not a problem to be solved.

447
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:39,920
You're a person who keeps discovering

448
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,720
life, learning and growing.

449
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,750
And that person deserves time,

450
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:48,950
attention and kindness.

451
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:53,080
Maybe today you don't have much energy.

452
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:56,270
Maybe your plans are moving more slowly than expected.

453
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:58,860
Or maybe you don't know exactly yet

454
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,470
what you want to do.

455
00:21:00,470 --> 00:21:01,880
That's okay.

456
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:05,060
You don't need to have all the answers.

457
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:07,420
You can start with one small thing that

458
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:09,120
means something to you.

459
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,080
A few minutes of French.

460
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,850
A sincere conversation.

461
00:21:12,850 --> 00:21:14,050
A moment of rest.

462
00:21:14,050 --> 00:21:15,690
A new habit.

463
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:19,150
Or simply deciding to speak to yourself with a

464
00:21:19,150 --> 00:21:20,990
little more gentleness.

465
00:21:20,990 --> 00:21:23,340
These are simple gestures.

466
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:27,600
But sometimes, it's these gestures that gradually change

467
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,080
the way we live.

468
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:33,440
Thank you for sharing this moment with me.

469
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:37,400
I hope this conversation gave you a few new French

470
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:40,570
expressions, a little calm and maybe an idea

471
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:42,130
to keep with you.

472
00:21:42,130 --> 00:21:45,040
Before you go, I'd like to ask you a question.

473
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:48,130
What's the best thing you've ever done

474
00:21:48,130 --> 00:21:50,320
to invest in yourself?

475
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:54,050
And what small thing would you like to start today?

476
00:21:54,050 --> 00:21:57,720
Tell me about your experience in the comments.

477
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,840
I'd be really happy to read you.

478
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:02,000
Take good care of yourself, my friend.

479
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,310
See you very soon on Cozy French Radio.

480
00:22:05,310 --> 00:22:07,080
See you soon.
